        ['How to read medical news', 'There is a long way between a headline and a cure. A study on cells or animals is not a therapy; an algorithm tested in one hospital may perform worse elsewhere; a company press release is not a scientific paper. That is why FAIND always names the outlet and links to the original article. <strong>These pages inform; they do not replace a doctor\'s advice.</strong>']
